&lt;p&gt;Build and own a self-service, multi-tenant platform that keeps the critical data of 20+ customers recoverable&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Do you like building platforms that other teams consume, at scale, across private and public clouds, with security and tenant isolation as non-negotiables? At Schuberg Philis, the world is shifting from traditional backup to data security and resilience. We’re looking for a Platform Engineer to strengthen our Data Management-as-a-Service (DMS) team and help us build the next generation of our platform.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;About the Team&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DMS team builds and runs a shared, fully segregated data resilience platform that serves more than 20 of our customers. Customer teams consume it through self-service, and they handle their own day-to-day backup and restore operations. That means you won’t spend your days on job monitoring, restore tickets or backup schedules. Your customers are internal and external engineering teams, and your product is the platform they build on.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll join a dedicated group of data security experts within our larger Services Team and work closely with our sbp.cloud team, who operate our self-built sovereign cloud solutions. With our plan-build-run approach, you take end-to-end ownership: you design it, you build it, you run it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Challenge&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Running one platform for 20+ customers means solving the hard problems of platform engineering:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-tenancy by design: strict isolation of data, access, and performance between customers, on shared infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-service at scale: APIs, guardrails and automation that let customer teams onboard and operate independently, without tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale and resilience: 4,000+ protected endpoints and more than 25,000 recovery points generated daily, on a dedicated private cloud spanning multiple availability zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Heterogeneous workloads: Oracle, MS-SQL, SAP, Sybase, PaaS, container platforms and VMs across VMware VCF, OpenStack, AWS, Azure and Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern storage back-ends: public cloud services and S3-compatible object storage built on Pure FlashBlade//S and NetApp StorageGRID in our own datacenters, plus a long-term archiving tier.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security first: immutability, segregation and hardening in a highly secure environment where recoverability is the ultimate guarantee.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Platform Engineer, you take full responsibility for the lifecycle of the platform: architecture, deployment, evolution and reliability. You treat the platform as a product: you improve features, drive innovation and keep the user experience of customer teams in mind. You work closely with technology vendors (primarily Commvault) and push their product teams to improve, while applying standardized guardrails, driving automation and following best-in-class practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your focus is on making day-2 operations simple and cost-effective, so there is room to implement new security features, streamline customer onboarding and enable new projects. You also guide customers in their data protection needs, contribute to RFIs/RFPs, and help scope and design new solutions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the architecture and lifecycle of a multi-tenant data resilience platform, in line with our plan-build-run methodology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and ship self-service capabilities that customer teams use independently, end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate everything repeatable: deployments, tenant onboarding, configuration and platform operations, using Infrastructure as Code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure platform availability, aiming for 100% uptime and maximum customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve a diverse storage back-end across public cloud and on-prem S3-compatible solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable customers to protect workloads on VMware VCF, OpenStack, AWS, Azure, Kubernetes and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with vendor product teams and drive their roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on advisory and technical support, contribute to RFI/RFP processes, and help design new solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who Are You?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First and foremost, you are a platform engineer at heart, and you like building things other engineers rely on. A passion for data protection, security and resilience is a plus, and you’ll grow it here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy teamwork, thrive on challenges and like collaborating with both peers and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable in highly secure, complex environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a solid understanding of multi-tenant architectures and security concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proficient in Linux and/or Windows ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience across private (VMware/OpenStack) and public cloud platforms (Azure, AWS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re skilled in Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, Ansible and/or Chef) and in scripting and automation (Python, Bash, PowerShell, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data management/protection tools is valuable, whether Commvault, Rubrik or similar, but not a must. We’ll teach you the domain; you bring the engineering craft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More information?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Do not hesitate to call Maggie: 06 23 75 70 86.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Only application submitted through the website will be considered.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion in the tech industry.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategic Account Executive, you will own a portfolio of our largest most strategic customers and prospects in Germany, helping them get the most value from GitLab’s AI-powered DevSecOps platform. You’ll break into net new enterprise accounts and expand GitLab’s footprint within existing customers, using a consultative approach to understand their business needs and guide successful adoption and expansion of GitLab. You’ll work closely with pre- and post-sales teams and strategic channel partners to drive full-cycle sales, from prospecting and qualification through rollout, usage, and long-term growth, while acting as the voice of your customers by feeding their feedback and product ideas into GitLab’s public issue tracker.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities-3&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and support GitLab’s Strategic account/(s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the end to end sales process through engagement of appropriate resources such as Solutions Architects, Customer Success Managers, Professional Services, Marketing, Executives, Partners, and the Channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage solution selling expertise to respond efficiently to customer needs and identify business potential in order to build a strategic, long-term partnership with your customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a deep understanding of the customer, including an understanding of their performance metrics and develops plans in anticipation of the customer’s business strategies and goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand knowledge of industry as well as the competitive posture of the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to root cause analysis on wins/losses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate lessons learned to the team, including account managers, the marketing team, and the technical team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide account leadership and direction in the pre- and post-sales process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct sales activities including prospecting and developing opportunities in Strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the successful rollout and adoption of GitLab products through strong account management activities and coordination with pre-and-post sales engineering and support resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize a consultative approach, discuss business issues with prospect and develop a formal quote, a written sales proposal or a formal sales presentation addressing their business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop an account plan to sell to customers based on their business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;requirements-2&quot;&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into highly complex organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated consistent results and overachievement of quota&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills; comfortable presenting to C-Level executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with solutions selling and positioning value to customers based on their needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of with Git, Software Development Tools, Application Lifecycle Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You share our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/values/&quot;&gt;values&lt;/a&gt;, and work in accordance with those values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use GitLab&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel if needed and comply with the company’s travel policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
